[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Data Attributes and Programmatic Initialization in Bootstrap"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Bootstrap provides two primary ways to interact with and control its JavaScript components: declarative initialization via HTML data attributes and programmatic initialization via JavaScript. Understanding both approaches is essential for building flexible and maintainable web applications."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Declarative Initialization Using Data Attributes"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"By default, Bootstrap allows you to use its plugins without writing a single line of JavaScript. This is known as declarative initialization. You simply add data-* attributes to your HTML elements, and Bootstrap's built-in event listeners handle the behavior."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"<button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#exampleModal">
  Launch demo modal
</button>"},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"data-bs-toggle: Tells Bootstrap which plugin to initialize (e.g., modal, dropdown, tooltip)."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"data-bs-target: Specifies the target element via a CSS selector to apply the action to."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Programmatic Initialization Using JavaScript"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"While data attributes are convenient, you often need more control over when and how components are initialized. Programmatic initialization allows you to instantiate components manually via JavaScript, pass custom configuration options, and call public methods."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"const myModalEl = document.getElementById('myModal');
const modal = new bootstrap.Modal(myModalEl, {
  keyboard: false,
  backdrop: 'static'
});

// Manually trigger the modal to show
modal.show();"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Passing Options via JavaScript vs Data Attributes"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can also pass configuration options using data attributes by prefixing option names with data-bs-, such as data-bs-keyboard="false". However, programmatic initialization is preferred when dealing with complex options, dynamic DOM elements, or when you need to invoke methods directly after instantiation."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Data Attributes: Best for static markup, simple configurations, and rapid prototyping."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Programmatic Initialization: Best for dynamic applications, component reuse, method chaining, and advanced event handling."}]
